Ladybird validates property descriptors for an observable array index
or its length. Defining an adopted style sheet runs the callbacks that
register its fonts. A descriptor without a value leaves the list alone.

Blink uses ObservableArrayExoticObjectHandler::TrapDefineProperty.
Gecko uses ObservableArrayProxyHandler::defineProperty, and WebKit
uses JSObservableArray::defineOwnProperty. Chrome 158.0.8127.37,
Firefox 151.0 and WebKit 26.5 all registered the replacement font.

Firefox and WebKit rejected definitions past the end and accepted empty
descriptors. Chrome reported success for a hole or length growth, and
threw for an empty descriptor on an index or length. Ladybird follows
Web IDL in these cases. WebKit retained the font after defining the
length as zero.
